{
  "summary": "This RNA-only experiment (single profile, scvi_n200) constitutes a clean single-variable swap relative to the PCA n2000 baseline (llm_summary_001), isolating the effect of a learned nonlinear latent representation versus linear dimensionality reduction. The scvi n200 configuration achieved a validation accuracy of 0.520 (F1: 0.498), a ~3.5-point improvement over PCA n2000 (0.485, F1: 0.464), suggesting that the learned scvi representation captures more predictive structure than PCA even at a substantially lower dimensionality (200 vs. 2000). It remains uncertain whether this encoder advantage persists in multimodal or multiprofile configurations, whether alternative learned encoders (e.g., scGPT) or different latent dimensions could yield further gains, and whether the observed improvement is stable across different random initializations."
}

